 Develop and execute payroll strategies, providing leadership and direction while implementing controls and process improvements to ensure accurate and timely payroll processing; 
 Ensure the accuracy and integrity of payroll transactions, maintain payroll-related system configurations, and support organizational financial reporting through effective payroll accounting and reporting practices; 
 Lead, develop, coach, and evaluate payroll team members in alignment with job expectations and Bethany's values; 
 Evaluate payroll technology solutions and serve as the Subject Matter Expert (SME) to maximize system capabilities, efficiency, and operational effectiveness; 
 Evaluate vendor solutions, as directed by organizational leadership, to ensure services meet Bethany's operational, compliance, and service requirements; 
 Serve as the point of escalation for complex payroll issues and partner with Finance, Human Resources, Information Technology, vendors, and organizational leadership to resolve concerns effectively; 
 Provide leadership and governance over payroll compliance by maintaining a continual pulse on evolving federal, state, and local payroll regulations; evaluating organizational risk; recommending policy, process, and system enhancements; and ensuring timely implementation of compliancerelated changes; 
 Lead and support special projects, strategic initiatives, operational reviews, and payroll-related data analyses and requests for the Chief Financial Officer, executive leadership, and key stakeholders to support process improvements, compliance efforts, and informed business decision-making; 
 Collaborate with Human Resources and Information Technology to ensure the accuracy, integrity, and security of employee and payroll-related data; 
 Serve as the Finance department SME on payroll operations, process improvements, strategic initiatives, and organizational planning efforts; 
 Oversee and support the annual Workers' Compensation audit and provide payroll data and analysis to support accurate employee classifications and reporting requirements; 
 Complete other duties as assigned. 
