 Bachelor’s level degree from an accredited college; 
 Certified Payroll Professional (CPP) accreditation preferred; 
 At least five (5) years of progressive experience managing and processing payroll operations; 
 At least two (2) years of experience managing a payroll operations team; 
 Working knowledge of configuration, functionality and implementation of payroll processing systems, UKG suite of products preferred; 
 Strong analytical, diagnostic, and problem-solving skills reflective of an understanding of the business implications of decisions; 
 Exercise a high level of confidentiality; 
 Excellent verbal and written communication skills; 
 Must be able to work with all levels of the organization and stakeholders; 
 Demonstrated strong customer service focus, allowing for the development of strong working relationships and collaboration with other departments to achieve desired outcomes; 
 Must be reliable with time sensitive deadlines and tasks; 
 Work well under pressure and adaptable to change; 
 Proficient in Microsoft Office, with advance use of Excel; 
 Familiarity with configuration, functionality and implementation of HRIS systems, UKG suite of products preferred; 
 Computer skills sufficient to perform essential functions including knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite; 
 Must be 21 years old with a valid driver's license with at least 3 years driving experience in the U.S. to operate a vehicle on behalf of Bethany; 
